# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the site's root (docs/deploy.md). Vite puts files whose
# names carry a content hash in /assets: they never change under the same name, so browsers
# keep them for a year. Nothing here sets a framing, referrer or content-security rule on
# purpose: the page frames YouTube's player and ChimpVibe's games, and YouTube's player needs
# to see which site is asking.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
